// Execute Commands on EC2 Instances via SSM (T1651)
//
// Discriminators: shell DOCUMENT, non-automation PRINCIPAL, and FAN-OUT across
// target instances. The original query matched three SSM event names with no
// qualifier at all, which is unusable - SendCommand and GetCommandInvocation
// are routine patching.
//
// Targeting has two shapes and both matter:
//   Req.instanceIds - explicit list; count it.
//   Req.targets     - tag-based selector. A broad tag target is fleet-wide
//                     regardless of how many explicit instances are named, so
//                     its mere presence is treated as fan-out.
//
// Dialect: Sentinel / Azure Log Analytics KQL. NOT CloudWatch Logs Insights.
AWSCloudTrail
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where EventSource == "ssm.amazonaws.com"
| where EventName == "SendCommand"
| extend Req = parse_json(RequestParameters)
| extend Doc = tostring(Req.documentName)
| where Doc in ("AWS-RunShellScript", "AWS-RunPowerShellScript")
| extend TargetCount = array_length(Req.instanceIds)
| extend HasTagTargets = isnotempty(Req.targets)
// REPLACE these with the roles in YOUR account that legitimately run SSM
// commands on instances. The placeholder values below match nothing, so until
// they are edited this rule fires on every patch cycle.
//
// `contains` (substring), NOT `has` (whole-term): a role path is delimited by
// a slash and hyphens, so `has` does not match it reliably.
| where UserIdentityArn !contains "role/REPLACE-ME-patch-automation"
      and UserIdentityArn !contains "role/REPLACE-ME-ssm-automation"
| project TimeGenerated, UserIdentityArn, Doc, TargetCount, HasTagTargets,
          SourceIpAddress, CommandId = tostring(parse_json(ResponseElements).command.commandId)
// Threshold is >= 3 (tune to your real maintenance-window batch sizes). A broad
// tag Targets is fleet-wide regardless of the explicit-instance count.
| extend Verdict = case(
    TargetCount >= 3 or HasTagTargets, "FLEET-WIDE SHELL EXECUTION - P0",
    "SHELL EXECUTION BY NON-AUTOMATION PRINCIPAL, review")
| order by TargetCount desc
//
// CommandId is the pivot into what actually ran: feed it to
// `aws ssm list-command-invocations --command-id <id> --details`, or query the
// SSM output logs. CloudTrail frequently omits the command body, so do not
// conclude the commands were benign from its absence.
